{"text": "PHILIP MORRIS\nUSA,\nINTER-OFFICE CORRESPONDENCE JAN ees\n\nRICHMOND, VIRGINIA\naR NNEBAt\n\nTo: + Files (Reference Cigarettes) pate: January 23, 1974\n\nFron: +L. F, Meyer\n\nsbiect: - Telephone Conversation with Dr. A. Spears of Lorillard\n\nI called Dr. A. Spears of Lorillard today to discuss various\naspects related to the preparation of reference cigarettes\nfor the University of Kentucky undertaken by Lorillard in\n1963. Dr. Spears provided the following information\n\n1, The original IRI cigarettes were made to an\n85.0 mm length specification, (Their machines\nwere adjusted to this length).\n\n2. The cigarettes were prepared on Mark VIII\nmakers with dense ends.\n\n3. All of their packaging materials - labels,\ncartons, and cases were supplied by:\n\nFederal Paper Board (Mr. Robert C. Sargent)\n75 Chestnut Ridge Road\nMontvale, New Jersey 07645\n\nAdditionally the dies for printing codes and\nbutt lengths on the rods were obtained from\nFederal Paper Board,\n\n: Dr. Spears will send any packaging specifications and the dies\nto us for our potential duplication, He was most cooperative\nand said he would supply any further information requested\n\nfut\ncc: Dr, H. Ry Wakehan\nMr. F. E. Resnik\nR. N. Thomson\nW. G. Lloyd\nMr. J. Fuller\nMr. W. E, Poorbaugh", "words": [{"text": "PHILIP", "x0": 334, "y0": 46, "x1": 385, "y1": 60, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "MORRIS", "x0": 396, "y0": 48, "x1": 449, "y1": 60, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "USA,", "x0": 375, "y0": 66, "x1": 410, "y1": 74, "conf": 22.0}, {"text": "INTER-OFFICE", "x0": 229, "y0": 77, "x1": 369, "y1": 90, "conf": 88.0}, {"text": "CORRESPONDENCE", "x0": 389, "y0": 78, "x1": 557, "y1": 91, "conf": 93.0}, {"text": "JAN", "x0": 596, "y0": 79, "x1": 624, "y1": 94, "conf": 16.0}, {"text": "ees", "x0": 636, "y0": 79, "x1": 662, "y1": 93, "conf": 11.0}, {"text": "RICHMOND,", "x0": 325, "y0": 106, "x1": 387, "y1": 116, "conf": 38.0}, {"text": "VIRGINIA", "x0": 399, "y0": 106, "x1": 457, "y1": 116, "conf": 38.0